    "created_at": "2018-09-07T15:11:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-07T15:11:41Z",
    "body": "> Are there other ways to cause documents to have about:srcdoc URLs, besides document.open()?\r\n\r\nA `javascript:'hello'` iframe in a srcdoc document?  Gecko doesn't implement the spec behavior for using the url of the page the `javascript:` url comes from for the url of the resulting document  so far,  so that hasn't bitten us yet.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
